<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arturo Prat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1848–1879</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arturo Prat was a Chilean naval officer and lawyer who commanded the old corvette Esmeralda at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-iquique">Battle of Iquique</a> on 21 May 1879, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-pacific">War of the Pacific</a>. When the Peruvian ironclad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huascar">Huáscar</a> rammed his ship, he leapt aboard the enemy vessel and was killed. His sacrifice made him Chile's greatest naval hero, and 21 May is commemorated as Navy Day.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arturo-prat.jpg" alt="Arturo Prat" width="320" height="456" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arturo_Prat_con_espada.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
